{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/556451-solar-archery-vs-thrown","id":556451,"title":"Solar Archery vs. Thrown","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-15T21:07:50-07:00","id":556451,"title":"Solar Archery vs. Thrown","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">While making a new Solar, something was bugging me. I'm trying to make someone who was a hunter before their Exaltation; you know, the kind of person who harries their prey with ranged attacks, trying to cripple and poison them before moving into melee for the kill. Here's my question: Would Archery or Thrown be more appropriate? Most of the &quot;crippling&quot; charms seem to be in the Thrown tree, but does that mean that there's no place for them in Archery?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm a bit embarrassed to ask this but... If I wanted to make a &quot;Gate of Babylon&quot; charm tree, would it be appropriate for that to build off of Summoning the Loyal Steel, or is that a bit too... weird for Solar charms? Sorcery maybe?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:33:47-07:00","id":556508,"title":"","content":"Based on your intentions, I would recommend Thrown for you as it will give you both at once. Cascade of Cutting Terror can simulate the effects of Gate of Babylon pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:40:56-07:00","id":556518,"title":"","content":"It depends on how your character hunted before the exaltation. The only thrown weapons that you could use to hunt I can think of, are a spear or a bolas, which are very different kinds of hunting from each other. That said I don't see a reason you couldn't homebrew a crippling tree in archery.<br /> <br /> Also,as a hunter, the idea that the goal of a hunter is to cripple or poison prey before moving in for the kill (prolonging its suffering) is a little unsettling. Most hunting actually uses skills that assassins would use. Camouflaging yourself, sitting still for long periods of time, and using one shot to kill your prey as quickly as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:40:24-07:00","id":556561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/556451-solar-archery-vs-thrown?p=556518#post556518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,as a hunter, the idea that the goal of a hunter is to cripple or poison prey before moving in for the kill (prolonging its suffering) is a little unsettling. Most hunting actually uses skills that assassins would use. Camouflaging yourself, sitting still for long periods of time, and using one shot to kill your prey as quickly as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... His tribe was not what you'd call &quot;nice&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T22:50:24-07:00","id":556564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/556451-solar-archery-vs-thrown?p=556518#post556518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on how your character hunted before the exaltation. The only thrown weapons that you could use to hunt I can think of, are a spear or a bolas, which are very different kinds of hunting from each other. That said I don't see a reason you couldn't homebrew a crippling tree in archery.<br /> <br /> Also,as a hunter, the idea that the goal of a hunter is to cripple or poison prey before moving in for the kill (prolonging its suffering) is a little unsettling. Most hunting actually uses skills that assassins would use. Camouflaging yourself, sitting still for long periods of time, and using one shot to kill your prey as quickly as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on what you're hunting. I mean crippling a dear before you kill it is probably more of an accident than necessity. On the other hand if you decide to get crazy and hunt a tyrant lizard I have to imagine the crippling is the only reason you're expecting to live long enough for poison to take effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T04:35:38-07:00","id":556735,"title":"","content":"Probably the big issue with adding a whole crippling tree to Archery is obviating Thrown by making it basically &quot;same effects as Archery with worse range.&quot;<br /> <br /> For your concept I might think of fighting with hatchets and javelins to wear down a mammoth or something. Maybe have an atlatl. <br /> <br /> Also, like, doesn't poisoning prey animals kind of defeat the purpose if you want to eat them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T07:53:14-07:00","id":556884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/556451-solar-archery-vs-thrown?p=556735#post556735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, like, doesn't poisoning prey animals kind of defeat the purpose if you want to eat them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! Children of the tribe were fed poisoned food from an early age; those who die from it weren't fit for life in the first place (or so the elders say). Those who survive build up an immunity to poisons of all kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T09:06:44-07:00","id":556968,"title":"","content":"Mithraditism is cool! Also this does help prevent your food stores from being raided by either man or beast, haha. <br /> <br /> What is the tribe's reason for maximizing suffering of animals though? That seems to be a thing that most groups IRL have historically tried to prevent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:15:27-07:00","id":557092,"title":"","content":"I forget, what charms for archery and thrown were merged and martial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:12:04-07:00","id":557233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/556451-solar-archery-vs-thrown?p=556968#post556968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithraditism is cool! Also this does help prevent your food stores from being raided by either man or beast, haha</div> </div> </div> </div>It also does other things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is the tribe's reason for maximizing suffering of animals though? That seems to be a thing that most groups IRL have historically tried to prevent. </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking they would be demon worshippers, which would explain where he got the majority of his sorcerous formulas. They were taught that the sweetness of suffering and fear offsets the bitter flavor of the poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":899,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","user":"The Free Man","date":". 06-16-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:25:13-07:00","id":557263,"title":"","content":"I'd say in some ways it'd be more interesting if they were worshiping a malign wood elemental or bog goddess or something (or Mother Bog). Demon-worship for suffering is a little cliche. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:43:47-07:00","id":557298,"title":"","content":"Ya know what? That sounds perfect. Thanks Zel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}